This is my fifth ascension overall, and the first time I've gotten
genoless conduct. I usually get polypileless conduct as well, but at
one point in this game I was so desperate for a bag of holding that I
gathered what magical tools I could find and polymorphed them a few
times. I got nothing useful out of that, but it did keep me from
getting polypileless. (I got polyselfless this time as usual as well).

Also I used a displacement cloak instead of a MC3 cloak; some people
seem to think that that counts as a "conduct", though it really didn't
make too much difference.

Kara started out with a pet cat Zephyr. Zephyr died fairly quickly,
and a succession of other cats and dogs followed; Boreas, Levanter,
and finally Mistral. Mistral polymorphed into a golden naga for
awhile, and later into an Elvenking. Mistral the Elvenking lasted
through much of the game, before drowning in Juiblex's swamp (oops).

Kara used a pickaxe and then a mattock for the first part of the game,
then was granted Grayswandir by Quetzlcoatl (or whoever), and wielded
it solo for quite awhile, before eventually finding a second saber and
dual wielding the two of them. They slice, they dice!

Kara found a cursed genocide scroll, and left it cursed for awhile,
since she had decided not to wipe anything out. Eventually she used it
to send in some storm giants, granted her a huge strength boost as
well as shock resistance, which she was having trouble finding
elsewhere (no blue dragons for quite awhile).

Aside from the early problems with not having a bag of holding, there
weren't too many problems. This was the first time I'd ever seen
Geryon in a game.. some random demon gated him in. He was peaceful for
awhile. I didn't attack him, but he got mad at something and tried to
attack me. He quickly regretted it as the silver sabers sliced through
him like those cheese slicing things through cheese.

Also this is the first time I'd seen Yeenoghu without specifically
summoning him. Again gated by a random demon, and again sliced into
quickly. (Actually, one of my first games of Nethack ever, I played an
arc in explore mode, and the Minion gated in Yeenoghu. The two of them
basically kicked my ass, even though I was invincible and all. But
this was the first time for the big Y in a real game.)

I wondered with all my luck at demon gating if I'd get the big D, but
he didn't show up. Neither did the little D (Dispater), who I was sort
of hoping for too.

This game was a few firsts for me.. first time I did a new conduct,
first time I really made use of a stash (and due to that, I was able
to ascend with a lot of loot), as well as the obvious first arc
ascension.

Kara was a pretty good spellcaster too... magic missile is great.

Alright. So I've done Val/Bar/Sam/Hea/Arc now. Who should be next...?

The voice of Quetzalcoatl booms out: "Congratulations,
